# Parallel Sessions: Shared Checkout + Test Queue

Canonical workflow: `docs/workflow/parallel-sessions.md`. Brief block and parent steps: skill `parallel-sessions` (`earnie-workspace/ai/skills/parallel-sessions/SKILL.md`).

## One checkout per line

- One clone per line (`main`, and one per open `release/x.y`); no `git worktree add` and no extra clone unless the user agreed in chat for that case.
- Parallel sessions on a line share its checkout. Never `git checkout` / `switch` branches there: other sessions and the user work in it.
- Work for another line (e.g. a cherry-pick onto `release/x.y`) belongs to that line's clone; point it out instead of doing it here.
- Regression triage: `run_regression --compare-at` creates and removes its own temporary worktree under `..\earnie-compare-wt` (skill `regression-triage`); that is the only worktree use.

## Child sessions

- Edit only the files / functions named in the brief; two sessions never edit the same function. Shared file: re-read it right before each edit.
- New tests go into a new test file of their own.
- Run only the new tests and the existing tests of the changed code: no full suite, no `scripts.run_regression`, no backtesting / SE runs.
- No commit, no push, no branch switch. Report changed files, targeted test result, open questions.

## Parent session

Wait for every child, check `git status` for foreign changes, run the full suite and `scripts.run_regression` once, send red tests back to the owning session, then ask the commit target once for all changes.

## Tests

- Always via `scripts.run_pytest` / `scripts.run_regression` — they queue machine-wide (`scripts/suite_queue.py`); never plain `python -m pytest`, never `EARNIE_TEST_QUEUE=off` / `--no-queue` to jump the queue.
- Full suite in Claude Code: Bash tool with `run_in_background: true` (queue wait + run can exceed the 10 min foreground limit). Targeted files/node ids (≤ 3) use the fast lane and do not queue.
- Waiting output `[test-queue] waiting …` is normal — do not kill and restart the run. `python -m scripts.suite_queue status` shows the queue.
- Shared `.venv`: dependency changes affect all sessions — coordinate with the user before installing.
